Chapter: GopHandoff

 The UEFI stub's handoff contract.

 handoff-magic is the eight ASCII bytes "CDXHANDF" read as one little-endian
 quadword, which is how the stub stores them.

 There used to be a second reading. option_a_stub.asm put a CELL_FB at 0x8000
 holding base/width/height/stride as four quadwords, while cdx-to-pe.ps1's stub
 puts the UEFI SystemTable at that same address, so a payload reading 0x8000
 unconditionally was right under one stub and read a SystemTable pointer as a
 framebuffer base under the other. **That stub was deleted 2026-08-03 and
 nothing can write a CELL_FB any more**, so the fallback that read 0x8000 when
 the magic was absent is gone with it: it could only ever fire on an image
 built by a builder that no longer exists, and what it would have returned is
 the SystemTable pointer, which is the exact confusion it was written to
 prevent.

 A zero base now means what it says. The stub writes the header
 unconditionally but jumps over the framebuffer body when LocateProtocol(GOP)
 returned nothing, so callers must still treat a zero base as "no
 framebuffer", which is also the answer when there is no block at all.

 We say:

Section: Block

  handoff-base : Integer = 126976

  handoff-magic : Integer = 5063257923364865091

  handoff-present : Integer -> Boolean
  handoff-present (dummy) = peek-qword handoff-base 0 == handoff-magic

 Width and height share the quadword at +0x18, stride and pixel format the
 one at +0x20, because the stub stores them as four 32-bit fields.

  handoff-fb-base : Integer -> Integer
  handoff-fb-base (dummy) =
    if handoff-present 0 then peek-qword handoff-base 16
    else 0

  handoff-w : Integer -> Integer
  handoff-w (dummy) = bit-and (peek-qword handoff-base 24) 4294967295

  handoff-h : Integer -> Integer
  handoff-h (dummy) = bit-shru (peek-qword handoff-base 24) 32

  handoff-stride : Integer -> Integer
  handoff-stride (dummy) = bit-and (peek-qword handoff-base 32) 4294967295

Section: Boot Framebuffer

  boot-fb-base : Integer -> Integer
  boot-fb-base (dummy) = handoff-fb-base 0

  boot-fb-w : Integer -> Integer
  boot-fb-w (dummy) = handoff-w 0

  boot-fb-h : Integer -> Integer
  boot-fb-h (dummy) = handoff-h 0

  boot-fb-stride : Integer -> Integer
  boot-fb-stride (dummy) = handoff-stride 0
